{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implements third filing #10952 at head 3f26e8c5, recut cleanly from d22565108 onto main. The adapter resolves actor names from the workspace's in-memory custody first at zero filesystem cost; on a miss it re-reads config.json once under a per-workspace serialisation so concurrent misses share one read, adopting the fresh record on success — re-read-on-miss rather than config-change detection or cache removal, because misses are rare and the hot path must stay off the disk. Failures stay apart: no match after the fresh read reports \"addresses no known actor\" while an unreadable custody record reports its own I/O error, and the start gate no longer refuses a session for a name added later. Mutation-sensitive tests TestAdapterResolvesActorAddedAfterSessionStart plus both cases pinned apart in the adapter wiring pass at this head. Gates: gofmt clean, go vet ./... clean, full go test ./... -count=1 green across 30 packages, race run over cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/app green.","body":{"branch":"request/mcp-late-actor-resolution","commit":"3f26e8c5d476e624b6963a76fa3d125280715711","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}